    },
    {
      "id": "claim_776a173065704b8c8498edd003f66d21",
      "statement": "A refused .mmfeatures costs one extraction rather than a database of wrong numbers, because MotionMatchingData.GetOrImportFeatureSet answers a false return by re-extracting the features and writing them back; anything thrown while reading is caught and reported the same way, since a file written for another configuration takes its string lengths and array sizes from the wrong offsets and dies before it runs out of bytes.",
      "evidence": [
